The Kernel type is not directly visible in the source files I have checked so far. To test the logging call in CreatePluginFromGrpcDirectory, I will create a minimal mock or stub of the Kernel type with a LoggerFactory property that returns a controllable ILoggerFactory. This will allow me to verify that the LogTrace call is made with the expected message.

I will submit a test file that:
- Mocks a Kernel instance with a LoggerFactory that returns a mock ILogger.
- Sets up the mock ILogger to return true for IsEnabled(LogLevel.Trace).
- Calls CreatePluginFromGrpcDirectory with a test directory and plugin directory name.
- Verifies that LogTrace was called with the expected message.

I will use Moq for mocking ILogger and ILoggerFactory.

